Package: pie-zfsroot
Architecture: darwin-arm64
Depends: libsystem, zfs (>= 2.4.1p1+ds1-2), blueberry-pie-os-init (>= 5),
 opendirectoryd (>= 3), rpi-firmware (>= 1.20260521+git20260601.12eeaa1+ds1-2)
Description: ZFS root and data sets, sealing and soft reboots
 The tools for a system whose root is a ZFS dataset: pie-root-setup,
 which init runs at boot to mount the data set, pie-seal and pie-unseal,
 pie-stage, softreboot, pie-boot and pie-data.
 .
 The root holds everything packages install. dpkg leaves out /private/var,
 /private/tmp, /Users, /Volumes, /cores and /usr/local, which are the data
 set, and keeps its database in the root.
